ric (crew), not willing to further education (adaptability). So strong reliability and decision, but communication and adaptability concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility), but regarded as arrogant (crew), relatively weak leadership (crew), also arrogant may affect cooperation. So good technical, responsibility, but crew cooperation issues.\n\nWe need to pick best overall fit. Candidate C seems strong reliability, decision, crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric may be serious for cockpit. Candidate B has stress and conscientious but uncooperative. Candidate A has leadership but unorganized and criticism. Candidate D has responsibility but arrogance.\n\nProbably Candidate C is strongest overall despite communication issues? But communication is critical. Egocentric and difficulty communicating could be safety risk. Candidate B's uncooperative also risk. Candidate A's unorganized may affect reliability. Candidate D's arrogance also risk.\n\nWhich is least concerning? Candidate C's communication difficulty may be mitigated? But egocentric and not willing to further education is concerning for adaptability.\n\nMaybe Candidate B: conscientious, stress, weather assessment, computer skills, but uncooperative and grumpy. That could affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, but arrogance and weak leadership.\n\nI think Candidate C's reliability and decision quality are top, and positive crew atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite communication difficulty. Might be best.\n\nThus I will vote Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: state recommendation, refer to discussion (none yet), give evidence: reliability 100%, correct decisions quickly, positive crew atmosphere, but note concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. Conclude still best overall.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote Candidate C."}
