r propose another. Let's evaluate using our own facts.\n\nOur notes:\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, unfriendly, eats unhealthily.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, regarded as pretentious, sometimes adopts wrong tone when communicating.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, excellent attention skills, puts concern for others above everything.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, professional communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nWe have reliability for C (100%). For others, not explicit but we have some hints: B is very conscientious (reliability). A leadership but unfriendly. D takes responsibility seriously.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress very well. D responds to unexpected events adequately. A unknown. C unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision. B good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. D solves problems extremely well, concentrates. C excellent attention skills.\n\nDecision quality: C makes correct decisions quickly. A can anticipate dangerous situations (maybe decision). D responds adequately.\n\nCrew cooperation: C puts concern for others above everything (positive). B sometimes wrong tone. A unfriendly. D regarded as loner, moody.\n\nCommunication: C difficulty communicating ideas. B sometimes wrong tone. A unfriendly. D maybe not.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously. C puts concern for others. A leadership. B conscientious.\n\nAdaptability: C not willing to further education (low). B pretentious maybe low adaptability. A eats unhealthily maybe low. D moody, loner maybe low.\n\nOverall, Candidate C has strong reliability, decision, crew concern, attention. Weakness: communication difficulty, egocentric, low adaptability.\n\nCandidate B has strong stress, reliability, technical (weather, computer), but communication tone issues, pretentious.\n\nCandidate D has strong problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but moody, loner, maybe poor crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate A has strong technical (spatial vision, complex connections), leadership, anticipates danger, but unfriendly, unhealthy.\n\nWhich is best? The panel must choose one. We can either support C or propose B as better due to stress handling and reliability, and maybe communication issues less severe? But C's communication difficulty could be critical. However C puts concern for others above everything, which may offset communication issues.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing Agent 1's recommendation. We can either agree and add more evidence, or challenge.\n\nLet's perhaps challenge slightly: While C's reliability is excellent, his communication difficulty and egocentric attitude could be safety risk, especially in long-distance flights where crew coordination is vital. Candidate B, on the other hand, handles stress well, is very conscientious (reliable), and has strong technical skills (weather assessment, computer). His communication tone issues are noted but perhaps less severe than egocentric behavior. Therefore I might shift my vote to Candidate B.\n\nWe need to support with facts: B handles stress very well, very conscientious, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills. Also mention concerns: pretentious, wrong tone.\n\nThus we can propose Candidate B as the better overall fit.\n\nWe must produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\". Provide PUBLIC_MESSAGE with reasoning.\n\nLet's craft."}
