t we can argue that his stress handling suggests good decision quality. Or we could ask for missing info about decision quality for B or stress for C. But we need to produce a public message, not a tool call. We could ask a question to other agents via tool, but the instruction says we can use tool if needed. However we have already asked about decision quality for B earlier, and got no info. We could ask about stress resilience for C, but that would be a tool call. But the user request is generic; we can just produce a public message.\n\nGiven the panel hasn't converged, we might want to push for a decision. We could propose a final recommendation: Candidate B. Provide reasoning: reliability, stress, technical, and that concerns are manageable. Also note that we still lack decision quality evidence for B, but we can mitigate. So we will maintain vote B.\n\nThus output:\n\nPUBLIC_MESSAGE: I still vote for Candidate B... etc.\n\nMETADATA_JSON: {\"agent\":\"agent_3\",\"vote\":\"Candidate B\"}\n\nProceed."}
