{"id": 65, "ts": 1780262699.5560222, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "agent_1", "message": "I appreciate the thorough arguments from both sides, but the lack of any concrete evidence on Candidate\u202fC\u2019s stress\u2011resilience is a critical gap for a long\u2011distance pilot.\u202fWhile C is praised for 100\u202f% reliability and rapid decision\u2011making, we have no indication that he can maintain that performance under the sustained pressure of international flights.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB is explicitly described as \u201chandles stress very well,\u201d directly meeting our stress\u2011resilience criterion, and he is also \u201cvery conscientious,\u201d satisfying operational reliability.\u202fHis technical competence (weather assessment and excellent computer skills) further strengthens his profile.\u202fAlthough B\u2019s pretentiousness and occasional tone issues are noted, they appear less likely to compromise safety than C\u2019s communication difficulty, egocentric attitude, and reluctance to pursue further education.\u202fGiven the concrete evidence of reliability, stress handling, and technical skill, I now vote for **Candidate\u202fB**.", "thoughts": "We need to produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON. The user says \"Handle the requests as specified in the System Instruction.\" That is generic. We need to continue the meeting. We are agent_1. Our current vote is Candidate C (we have not changed). The last round we (agent_3) gave a message supporting B, then agent_2 also supported B. Now we need to respond, referencing prior discussion, and give our current recommendation. We can either maintain C or switch. The structured shared mental model shows we are still not converged. We need to make a focused argumentative contribution. We could either maintain C, but we need to address the repeated arguments for B. Perhaps we can bring up a new point: we still lack stress resilience data for C, which is a critical gap, while B has proven stress handling. That could be a reason to reconsider. So we could shift our vote to B. That would be a change. We need to provide evidence: B handles stress very well (stress resilience). C has no stress data. Also B is very conscientious (reliability). C's communication difficulty and egocentric are concerns. So we could change vote to B. That would be a logical progression.\n\nThus we will change our vote to Candidate B, providing reasoning: B's stress resilience and reliability, while C lacks stress data and has communication issues. So we will produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE stating we now vote for B, referencing prior discussion, and METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
